{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"In contrast, during turning freeze, there was an increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.048) and a decrease in M1-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.043) during the TurnStart phase (Fig. 3B).\",\n    \"The increased coherence between the PMC and STN may reflect a compensatory mechanism to maintain motor control in the face of disrupted cortical signals; however, this abnormal coupling could also contribute to the rigidity and motor impairments characteristic of FOG31,32.\",\n    \"We observed an increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence during TurnPre in normal turning, suggesting the role of PMC-STN connectivity in the initiation of the turning task.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"During normal turning, significantly higher PMC-STN alpha coherence was observed in the TurnPre phase (p = 0.0045, Fig. 3A).\",\n    \"In contrast, during turning freeze, there was an increase in PMC-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.048) and a decrease in M1-STN alpha coherence (p = 0.043) during the TurnStart phase (Fig. 3B).\",\n    \"Our analysis revealed that the decreases in the PMC alpha power (β = 0.154, p = 0.035) (Fig. 4A) and increases in PMC-STN alpha coherence (β = 0.205, p = 0.006) (Fig. 4B) during the TurnPre phase, but not the TurnStart phase, significantly predicted the freezing duration within the trial.\",\n    \"PMC alpha power reduction during the TurnPre phase (but not during the TurnStart phase) relative to walking positively correlated with freezing duration (β = 0.154, p = 0.035).\",\n    \"Increased PMC-STN alpha coherence during the TurnPre phase (but not during the TurnStart phase) relative to walking predicted shorter freezing episodes (β = 0.205, p = 0.006).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的核心事实有全文依据：冻结转弯期间，PMC-STN alpha coherence相对于步行基线确实在TurnStart阶段增加（p=0.048），同时M1-STN alpha coherence下降（p=0.043）。论文讨论也确实提出了两种可能解释：PMC-STN coherence增加可能反映维持运动控制的代偿机制，也可能与FOG相关的运动障碍有关。因此，不能判定报告完全错误。但是，报告将TurnStart阶段的结果作为H4与H5竞争性假说的主要依据，却省略了会影响解释的重要时间相位和临床关联。首先，正常转弯时PMC-STN alpha coherence已经在TurnPre阶段显著增加（p=0.0045）；冻结转弯时的TurnStart阶段增加被论文描述为延迟且伴随M1-STN alpha coherence解耦。其次，预测分析明确显示，TurnPre阶段PMC-STN alpha coherence增加与更短的冻结持续时间相关（β=0.205，p=0.006），而TurnStart阶段的coherence变化没有显著预测作用。再次，TurnPre阶段PMC alpha功率下降与更长的冻结持续时间相关（β=0.154，p=0.035）。这些结果意味着，PMC-STN alpha coherence不能简单概括为TurnStart阶段的耦合增强，其不同阶段的变化具有不同的行为关联。尤其是TurnPre阶段的coherence增加可能具有保护性或代偿性意义，而冻结期间延迟至TurnStart的增加则具有不同的病理背景。指控者对全文结果的描述准确，judge_supported应为yes。最终判断：报告并非捏造结果，其TurnStart发现及两种可能解释均有依据，但由于遗漏关键的TurnPre结果及其与冻结持续时间的关系，整体概括不完整，并可能改变读者对代偿性与病理性耦合的理解，因此report_supported为partly，而非yes。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "c672d48c-4919-49c8-80f9-b1bbf41ce3d8", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T125530764174Z", "elapsed_seconds": 43.547, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T12:56:14.321051+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "dbf076dc02b48cd425b80e11d182d48ba84c224cf9d0fcb4f4dbd80a160fe270", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chat